{"tool_name":"rosettabackrub","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rosettabackrub","home":"http://kortemmelab.ucsf.edu/backrub","summary":"The RosettaBackrub server computes near-native conformational ensembles from a single input protein structure in PDB format using the Backrub method.","addition_date":"2017-03-25T12:40:39Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:56Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rosettabackrub","credit":[{"name":"Feedback Form","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://kortemmeweb.ucsf.edu/backrub/wiki/Feedback"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://kortemmeweb.ucsf.edu/backrub/wiki/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein model validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0321"},{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"},{"term":"Protein modelling (backbone)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0479"},{"term":"Protein modelling (mutation)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0331"},{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}]}],"name":"RosettaBackrub","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"The RosettaBackrub server (http://kortemmelab.ucsf.edu/backrub) implements the Backrub method, derived from observations of alternative conformations in high-resolution protein crystal structures, for flexible backbone protein modeling. Backrub modeling is applied to three related applications using the Rosetta program for structure prediction and design: (I) modeling of structures of point mutations, (II) generating protein conformational ensembles and designing sequences consistent with these conformations and (III) predicting tolerated sequences at protein-protein interfaces. The three protocols have been validated on experimental data. Starting from a user-provided single input protein structure in PDB format, the server generates near-native conformational ensembles. The predicted conformations and sequences can be used for different applications, such as to guide mutagenesis experiments, for ensemble-docking approaches or to generate sequence libraries for protein design. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2010. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Friedland G.F."},{"name":"Humphris E.L."},{"name":"Kortemme T."},{"name":"Lauck F."},{"name":"Smith C.A."}],"citationCount":84,"date":"2010-05-12T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"RosettaBackrub-a web server for flexible backbone protein structure modeling and design"},"pmid":"20462859"}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein folding, stability and design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0130"},{"term":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rosettabackrub/web/kortemmelab.ucsf.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":57,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2013"},{"count":4,"year":"2016"},{"count":4,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2015"},{"count":5,"year":"2023"},{"count":6,"year":"2014"},{"count":6,"year":"2018"},{"count":6,"year":"2021"},{"count":8,"year":"2017"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkq369","pmcid":"PMC2896185","pmid":"20462859","ref_count":53,"refs":[{"count":1,"